#
# Counter-example for math:AnalyticPropertyBackedConstraint: a math:AnalyticProperty
# individual that carries NO math:definingLaw — a bare analytic-property claim backed by
# neither a real first-order logic:Formula nor an honest logic:expressivenessBoundary.
# An analytic property is a quantified statement about a function's values, never a bare
# flag. The class-guarded existence lowers to a sh:sparql constraint, so validation MUST
# emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:UnbackedAnalyticProperty).
# Bound by ex:ecAnalyticPropertyUnbacked.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:bareAnalyticClaim a math:AnalyticProperty .
